{
 "schema": "opentallas.qwen3-8b-deployment-quality.v1",
 "purpose": "Finding 4 of docs/ARCHITECTURE_ATLAS_FEASIBILITY_REVIEW_2026_09_27.md (untracked review): full-model Qwen3-8B quality under the deployment weight format, KV format, accumulation order, normalisation and attention arithmetic, each deviation alone and combined, against the vendor BF16 GPU arithmetic.",
 "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-8B (HF snapshot, 36 layers, hidden 4096, 32/8 heads, head_dim 128, vocab 151,936), full model, not a reduced vehicle",
 "tool": "tools/qwen3_deployment_quality.py",
 "test": "tests/test_qwen3_deployment_quality.py",
 "deployment_arithmetic_sources": {
  "weights_3p5_bit": {
   "stated_point": "3.5 bits/parameter: configs/hardware/technology.json:1362 (reference_parts.taalas_hc1.weight_bits_per_parameter, 'custom 3-bit base type ... combining 3-bit and 6-bit parameters', mix ratio unpublished); tools/arch_budget_qwen3.py:55,85 (weight_bits=3.5); docs/ARCH_SPEC_QWEN3.md:47,93",
   "exact_quantiser_in_repo": "NONE. The atlas lists it as pending ('Pending - Qwen3-8B weight and KV formats ... token agreement and accuracy of the full quantised model ... are open. Settled by: a quantised golden'); no group size, scale format or codebook is specified anywhere for Qwen3.",
   "emulated_as": "q35: symmetric INT3 (codes -4..3) and INT6 (-32..31) groups of 128 along K, one BF16 scale per group, per-group MSE-optimal clip (21 ratios 0.5..1.0), the 12.5% of groups of each matrix with the largest INT3->INT6 squared-error reduction at INT6: 3 + 0.125*3 + 16/128 = 3.500 bits/parameter. Data-free round-to-nearest (no GPTQ/AWQ calibration). All linear layers including lm_head; the embedding table stays BF16. Brackets: w4 (INT4 g128, 4.125 b) and w3 (INT3 g128, 3.125 b). In contract mode the quantised matrix is the norm-folded W' = bf16(W diag(w)); in gpu mode the original W.",
   "activations": "BF16 (the golden rounds every matrix input to BF16, tools/hdc_golden.py@8a91421a:108-118); the HC1 reference's assumed 8-bit activations (technology.json taalas_hc1.execution_format, 'w4a8') are NOT adopted by the Qwen golden and are not emulated"
  },
  "kv_fp8": "tools/hdc_golden.py@8a91421a:257-276 (to_fp8: E4M3, bias 7, max 448 saturating, subnormal quantum 2^-9, RNE, canonical +0; kv_round default fp8 when HDC_SU_WIDTH>1). Per-element, NO scale (no per-tensor/per-head/per-block scale exists in the golden). Applied to K after q/k-norm and RoPE, and to V. Commit 8a91421a is on side branches (codex/qwen-coupled-schedule and others), not an ancestor of main fb12a089, whose tools/hdc_golden.py still keeps a BF16 KV cache.",
  "accumulation": "tools/hdc_golden.py@8a91421a: matvec 108-118 (BF16 input; K cut into split_for(N,K,G) contiguous chunks, each sequential from +0, chunk sums a pairwise tree); split_for 121-133 at G = 8,192 lane groups (tools/arch_budget_qwen3.py:62 GROUPS_ROM) gives chunk lengths qkv 8 (S=512), o 16 (S=256), gate/up 32 (S=128), down 48 (S=256), lm_head 2 (S=2048); attention attn_splits 140-150 + matvec_il 153-171: scores 128-way interleaved over head_dim (a pure pairwise tree of 128 exact products), P.V 1,024-way interleaved over positions (chunks of ceil(T/1024) sequential terms, then a 1,024-leaf pairwise tree); stream-unit sums (norm sums of squares, softmax Z) reduce_chunked 191-213 (R-ARITH chunk 8 + pairwise tree padded with +0). NOTE: at the Qwen3 spec shape the weight dot products are NOT uniformly 'chunk-8' as atlas section 6.5 states for V4.1; the chunk length is K/split_for.",
  "fp_units": "IEEE binary32 RNE add and mul, canonical +0 (8a91421a:84-106; rtl ot_fp32_add_rne_pipe / ot_fp32_mul_rne_pipe). The 3-cycle FP-unit latency is a timing property and does not change values.",
  "normalisation": "RMSNorm weight folded into the q/k/v and gate/up columns in BF16 with 1/rms applied after the product (8a91421a:282-301, NORM_FOLD when SU_WIDTH>1); rsqrt = seed 0x5F3759DF - (bits>>1) + 3 Newton steps (226-233; rtl/hdc/ot_hdc_sfu.sv); q/k-norm and final norm unfolded (299-301)",
  "attention_and_special_functions": "q and unnormalised probabilities rounded to BF16 before their products; one-pass softmax: row max, e = exp(s - max), P.V of e, then x 1/Z (attend 323-331); exp = rint(x log2e) by the 1.5*2^23 trick + two-constant Cody-Waite + degree-6 Horner + exponent add, clamp [-87, 88] (243-255); reciprocal = seed 0x7EF311C7 - bits + 3 Newton steps (235-241; rtl/hdc/ot_hdc_sfu.sv:105-122); silu = g * reciprocal(1 + exp(-g)) (334-336); RoPE tables fp32 angle, float64 cos/sin rounded once (304-316)"
 },
 "contract_emulation_fidelity": "Exact, not approximated: the GPU contract forward (Triton chunk + binary-counter pairwise-tree kernel; eager FP32 golden primitives) reproduces the numpy golden (tools/hdc_golden.py@27d30c15, blob 9c1640f9) bit-exactly in every logit of the reduced Qwen3 vehicle at groups 1, 4, 64, 1,024 and 8,192, BF16 and FP8 KV, including blocked prefill and batched decode of sequences of different lengths (tests/test_qwen3_deployment_quality.py). Every product is exact in FP32 (BF16 x BF16, E4M3 x BF16, or INT<=6 x BF16 scale x BF16 <= 21 significant bits), so the kernel's FMAs equal the golden's separate mul + add. All 36 layers and the lm_head run in the contract order; nothing is sampled by layer.",
 "gpu_reference_fidelity": "a_bf16 re-implements HF transformers Qwen3 BF16 arithmetic; WikiText-2 window-0 NLL 1.98450 vs HF transformers 4.57.6 sdpa 1.98450 (raw_hfcheck), i.e. PPL 7.2754 both.",
 "evaluation_protocol": {
  "wikitext2": "Salesforce/wikitext wikitext-2-raw-v1 test, '\\n\\n'.join, Qwen tokenizer (299,078 tokens), non-overlapping windows of 2,048 and 8,192, every position scored; PPL = exp(mean NLL). CIs: paired bootstrap over windows (2,000 resamples).",
  "greedy": "first 50 MT-bench first-turn prompts, Qwen chat template with enable_thinking=False, 256 greedy tokens (no EOS stop), each prompt prefilled alone and the 50 decoded together; 'free run' compares each mode's own continuation with a_bf16's (first divergent index); 'teacher forced' re-scores a_bf16's continuation and counts positions whose argmax equals a_bf16's token (cluster bootstrap over prompts).",
  "mmlu": "cais/mmlu all/test, 1,000 questions sampled with numpy seed 0, zero-shot 'Answer:' prompt, argmax over the ' A'..' D' logits; CI bootstrap over questions, delta paired."
 },
 "modes_legend": {
  "a_bf16": "reference: vendor BF16 GPU arithmetic, BF16 weights, BF16 KV",
  "a_bf16_unbatched": "the same reference with each greedy prompt decoded alone instead of in a batch of 50: the GPU BF16 run-to-run noise floor for greedy divergence",
  "b_wq35": "(b) weight format only: q35 RTN (3.500 bits) in the GPU arithmetic",
  "b_gptq35": "(b') the same 3.500-bit format, GPTQ-calibrated (C4, 128 x 2048 tokens), GPU arithmetic",
  "b_w4": "bracket: INT4 g128 RTN (4.125 bits), GPU arithmetic",
  "b_w3": "bracket: INT3 g128 RTN (3.125 bits), GPU arithmetic",
  "c_kvfp8": "(c) KV format only: per-element FP8 E4M3 KV, GPU arithmetic, BF16 weights",
  "d_contract": "(d) arithmetic contract only: golden order/normalisation/attention/special functions, BF16 weights, BF16 KV",
  "f_contract_kvfp8": "(c)+(d): the whole deployment arithmetic except the weight format",
  "e_full": "(e) all combined: contract + q35 RTN (norm-folded) + FP8 KV",
  "e_full_gptq": "(e') all combined with GPTQ-calibrated q35 (norm-folded, calibrated on the contract's normalised-without-weight inputs)"
 },
 "gptq": "GPTQ (Frantar et al. 2022), block = group = 128, 1% dampening, no act-order, per-group MSE-clip scale chosen on the error-updated weights at the group start, INT3/INT6 group allocation as RTN (weight-space); sequential layer-by-layer on C4 en train shard 00000 (128 random 2,048-token segments, seed 0) through the vendor BF16 forward with already-quantised earlier matrices; lm_head included. Built in-process, never written to disk.",
 "not_run": [
  "C4 perplexity (WikiText-2 only).",
  "GSM8K (MMLU 1,000-question zero-shot subset is the downstream task).",
  "Contract-mode 8K perplexity on 16 of the 36 WikiText-2 8K windows (131,056 scored tokens); GPU modes use all 36. Every 8K delta is paired over the same windows.",
  "e_full_w4 (contract + INT4 + FP8 KV): started, stopped to give the GPU to the GPTQ runs.",
  "Activation-aware or rotation-based quantisers (AWQ, QuaRot/SpinQuant, codebooks), mixed-precision search with activation statistics, and quantisation-aware training: the 3.5-bit results are for RTN and GPTQ only, so they bound what a stronger 3.5-bit format could reach from below, not from above.",
  "A per-head or per-block scaled FP8 KV variant (the golden has none; per-element unscaled E4M3 was already within noise).",
  "8-bit activations (the HC1 reference's assumed 'w4a8'): not in the Qwen golden, not emulated."
 ],
 "conclusion": {
  "arithmetic_contract": "ACCEPTABLE. The golden order (split_for trees at 8,192 groups, interleaved attention trees, chunk-8 stream sums), norm fold, Newton rsqrt/reciprocal, Cody-Waite exp and one-pass softmax change WikiText-2 perplexity by -0.14% (2K) and -0.09% (8K), i.e. slightly better than BF16, MMLU -0.3 pt [-0.7, 0.0], and 98.3% top-1 agreement whose disagreements sit on exact BF16 logit ties (median reference margin 0.0). These figures use the implemented contract's reciprocal saturation (reciprocal_saturation; golden and RTL at 27d30c15).",
  "fp8_kv": "ACCEPTABLE. Per-element unscaled E4M3 KV changes perplexity by -0.19% (2K) / -0.14% (8K), MMLU -0.4 pt [-1.4, 0.6]; 96.6% top-1 agreement, disagreements at near-ties (94% with reference margin < 0.5 logit). Contract + FP8 KV together (f_contract_kvfp8): -0.16% / -0.09%, MMLU -0.3 pt.",
  "weights_3p5_bit": "NOT ACCEPTABLE as realised here. 3.5 bits/parameter costs +49% perplexity RTN / +14% GPTQ in the GPU arithmetic, and +41% RTN / +23% GPTQ (2K), +30% GPTQ (8K) combined with the contract and FP8 KV; MMLU -10.6 pt (RTN) / -7.5 pt (GPTQ) combined. Even INT4 g128 RTN (4.125 bits) costs +9.2% perplexity and -5.8 pt MMLU. The weight format, not the arithmetic contract, is the whole quality loss.",
  "combined_deployment": "NOT ACCEPTABLE against the stated threshold (<= +2% perplexity at every context and <= 1.0 pt MMLU drop): e_full +40.7% / +39.0% PPL, -10.6 pt MMLU; e_full_gptq +22.7% / +29.6% PPL, -7.5 pt MMLU. Greedy output diverges from BF16 within the first 1-2 tokens (median) on essentially every prompt, and at 8K 23.6% (GPTQ) / 30.0% (RTN) of teacher-forced top-1 tokens at positions 6,144-8,191 differ from BF16 (BF16 GPU noise floor for comparison: 72% of prompts diverge in free-run greedy within 256 tokens, median first divergence 101.5).",
  "what_would_change_it": "A quantiser that reaches <= 2% at ~3.5-4 bits on Qwen3-8B (activation-aware/rotation-based/codebook formats or QAT) must be demonstrated with this tool's contract mode (--wfile), or the ROM budget must carry more weight bits (the rate and energy figures quoted at 3.5 bits do not have a quality-preserving format behind them yet)."
 },
 "threshold": {
  "rule": "acceptable iff, against a_bf16, WikiText-2 perplexity rises by at most 2.0% (relative) at every measured context AND MMLU accuracy falls by at most 1.0 point (point estimates; the 95% CIs are reported beside them). Fixed before any full-model result was seen.",
  "ppl_rel_max": 0.02,
  "mmlu_drop_max_pt": 1.0
 },
